      "raw": "<p style=\"margin:0in 0in 8pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">Easy Mint.&nbsp; Especially with Legacy base power burying Meteor Storm right before the rest of the team deals damage.</span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:0in 0in 8pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">This was the first time I played FF Legacy on Mars, so I didn’t know how unfair late game is there.</span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:0in 0in 8pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">With him 1<sup>st</sup> in party once there is only a Meteor Storm or two left in environment deck it will make you immune to damage during villain turn then Legacy buries it, the rest of your team beats on the villain cards then environment plays it again and you are immune for the villain turn again, repeat indefinitely.</span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:0in 0in 8pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">It was like a Thunderstorm and all the minions and Voss were scared dogs while the heroes laughed it off.</span></span></span></p>",
